# tape037 (commit 93c017bd0) measured 14.33..14.53 tok/s on 512-token answers [measured]; a 2048-token answer
# reads deeper KV, so the band opens below [derived].
kind: baseline
question: what does one long MiniMax-M3 tape (Korean, n-predict 2048) show on the RTX A6000 with host experts
  at the serving defaults?
term: decode tok/s of the K3 tape (Korean, n-predict 2048), thinking as the template gives it, RTX A6000 +
  host experts, serving defaults
unit: tok/s
predict: 13.0..15.0
condition: one lease, the box quiet, the A6000 (BLOOMERY_CARD=a6000), a fresh server, two discarded warm-ups,
  io pressure some avg10 under 5 before the tape, greedy
reason: the release post's MiniMax tape was too short; this is its long replacement
decide-in: publish it as the post's MiniMax tape
decide-below: under 13.0: deeper context or the host read costs more than tape037 showed; read the plan lines
  before publishing
decide-above: beyond 15.0: read the plan lines (more experts on the card than tape037's)
